WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.720
17 older Australians a day died last year, still waiting for home care. This is Omni View Asia Pacific, episode 16. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. ABC News puts the year's toll above 6400 people who died before home care arrived. That is up by more than a third from the year before. The people in that count were still in the queue. Across the region, Kim Yo Jong rejected Seoul's medical equipment offer on Thursday.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:32.500
The South China Morning Post carries her KCNA statement.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.880
She is the sister of Kim Jong-un.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.860
This is separate from the ballistic missile launch reported on October 7.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.020
She called the package a political provocation and a breach of sovereignty.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:48.780
She attacked Seoul for making public its bid for United Nations sanctions exemptions, referring

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:53.840
to scarce medicines, scarce equipment, and worsening health conditions was in her words

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.340
as reported, an insult.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:01:00.320
She cast the offer as a show of Southern Goodwill set against a northern refusal.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:07.200
The post reports her line that there is nothing to give or receive, and that respect is what she demands if ties are to mend.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:16.220
A study out Thursday from the Center for Global Development finds China's money for multilateral development institutions up 10 fold since 2010.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:18.580
The Straits Times reports the figures.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:25.340
Development Bank funding hit $3 billion in 2024. Money for UN development-related bodies

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:33.860
rose 47%. Climate finance through multilateral channels reached $5.25 billion in 2025. Support

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:40.460
for Gavi was cut 32%. Co-author Ian Mitchell calls the rise a big step from 15 years ago

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:48.560
and still a tiny slice of the Chinese economy, and he calls the choices selective. Co-author

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:53.740
to the World Health Organization, arriving as the United States left, do not close every

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:59.420
hole left by Washington and other Western cuts. China's World Bank share sits near 6 percent,

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:05.680
under half the formula. The United States keeps a veto near 16 percent. Western officials have

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:10.980
blocked a share shift, pointing to no consensus and to what they call a lack of Chinese transparency.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:18.000
Also today, China finished the new Yali River Bridge at Dandong in 2014. North Korea left

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.900
its side unfinished for 12 years.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:25.420
Work restarted after Xi Jinping's June visit, and neither Capitol has named an opening day,

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:27.040
the Straits Times reports.

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:33.420
In Bishnor, Uttar Pradesh, Babaram, Udaivir, and Mahendra died after a man drove a tractor

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.260
into a crowd.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.400
Circle officer Desdipak Singh told The Hindu.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:44.980
Vijayapura police have filed an FIR against MLA Basanaguda Patil Yatinal, expelled by the BJP

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:46.240
in March 2025.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:51.840
After vendor Abdul-Rizok Bhagwan alleged fake death certificates were used to pull his name,

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:56.080
and other names, off-Karnataka roles in the special intensive revision.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:02.020
In Victoria, an AI-made video put out in One Nation's campaign has prompted a push

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:06.940
to ban election deepfakes, the Sydney Morning Herald reports. In the wider world,

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:12.020
a US court has refused bail to a woman accused of filming Taiwan's leader's son for Beijing.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:17.920
Magistrate Judge Steve Kim ordered warning Heather Zong held on Wednesday, the South China

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:19.060
morning post reports.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:23.700
Her lawyers had tried to keep her out of jail and said she looks forward to proving innocence

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:24.420
at trial.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:29.460
They say the allegation is one day of surveillance in Seattle, not proof she would flee.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:33.060
Prosecutors told the judge her parents and siblings live in China.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:35.160
She is accused, not convicted.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:40.060
The case on both sides is whether Europe should answer China's export surge with tariffs

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:41.900
and tougher market access demands.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.700
Parliament voted Wednesday, 454-86,

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.920
for a resolution built around economic reciprocity

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:52.000
and a proportionate reply if Chinese markets stay shut.

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:54.820
Commission Envoy Maroche-Sef-Chovitch

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:56.200
is in Beijing on Thursday

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.940
for two days with Commerce Minister Wang Wen-Tao.

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:01.700
He had set an October deadline to shrink a gap

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.780
put at 360 billion euros,

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:05.960
about 410 billion dollars,

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:07.920
more than a billion dollars a day.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:14.180
For pressure, Belgian lawmaker Hill Devoutmans, who led the resolution, said Europe has economic

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:16.640
power and the moment to use it has come.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:22.520
France's high commission for strategy and planning in February urged fast steps, including

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:27.800
30% tariffs on many Chinese exports and a weaker euro against China's currency.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:33.320
Associated press reporting says politicians and economists across the block treat Chinese

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:38.800
subsidies and goods redirected after U.S. tariffs as a major threat to steel and car plants.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:44.300
For caution, that same report says it is still unclear what the EU can or will do.

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:46.880
German car sales are plummeting in China.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.880
Subsidized Chinese cars are set to undercut European makers on price,

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.760
and Volkswagen has already had mass layoffs.

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:57.540
France and Germany, in a letter the Associated Press said it had seen,

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:00.280
asked for a sweeping rethink of China policy.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:05.280
Both camps accept the size of the gap, China's rank as the block's second-largest trading

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.560
partner, and the shift of goods toward Europe after US tariffs.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:13.960
The dated next step in the reporting is that two-day meeting in Beijing, inside the October

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:14.360
deadline.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:19.720
A sign of progress, on the Prime Minister's account, is a finished National 5G map.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:25.520
Narendra Modi said on Thursday at the 10th India Mobile Congress, at Yashobumi in New Delhi,

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:31.160
that 5G now reaches every district. Open magazine carries the speech. He put the

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:36.160
base station count above 5-lock 50,000. He said mobile internet speeds are 10

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:41.120
times what they were in 2022. Through direct benefit transfer, he said 50

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:45.060
lock-core rubies reach beneficiaries and keeping money from what he called

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:50.920
wrong hands saved about 5-lock-core rupees. Under PM Kisan, he said, more than

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:54.040
In four lot-core rupees went straight into Farmer's bank accounts.

